# qqq IDE — Make everything pasteable. Orchestrate ideas. Turn the IDE into an operating system.

qqq IDE is an open-source VS Code / Code-OSS / VSCodium based project.

Its core idea is simple:

> Make everything pasteable.

qqq lets you paste images, files, folders, HTML pages, videos, and media directly into the editor — with WYSIWYG preview.

But qqq is not only about paste.

Paste is just the entry point.

The real goal is to create a new way to orchestrate ideas inside the IDE.

## Why qqq exists

Modern IDEs are becoming more than code editors.

For many developers, writers, creators, and AI tool users, the IDE is already the main workspace.

It is where we write code, collect references, manage files, talk to AI, read documentation, organize projects, and build ideas.

But one basic action is still too limited:

> Paste.

Most editors treat paste mainly as text.

qqq extends paste into a universal action.

With qqq, the IDE can receive real materials directly:

* images
* screenshots
* files
* folders
* HTML pages
* web images
* videos
* media resources
* documents
* mixed creative materials

The goal is to reduce the distance between seeing something, capturing it, organizing it, and using it.

## What qqq does

qqq makes many kinds of content pasteable and previewable inside the editor.

You can paste images, files, folders, HTML, videos, and media directly into VS Code / Code-OSS / VSCodium.

This works not only in Markdown.

qqq is designed to support plain text files, custom file extensions, and even files without extensions.

The workflow is simple:

> Copy. Paste. Preview. Organize. Continue.

## Why this matters

When an idea appears, the tool should not interrupt the idea.

You should not need to open another app, upload files somewhere, convert formats, manually move resources, or rebuild context before continuing.

qqq tries to make the IDE behave more like an operating environment for ideas.

That is why the direction of qqq is:

> Make everything pasteable.
> Create a new way to orchestrate ideas.
> Turn the IDE into an operating system.

## Core features

### Paste Everything

Paste images, files, folders, HTML pages, videos, and media directly into the editor.

### WYSIWYG Preview

qqq makes pasted content visible and usable inside the editor, instead of leaving everything as invisible paths or plain text references.

### Roam File Explorer

qqq includes a built-in file explorer called Roam.

Roam is designed for fast navigation, recent locations, keyboard-first workflows, quick file creation, and access to directories outside the current project folder.

### Media and document workflow

qqq supports workflows around:

